In triangle $OAB$, $\overrightarrow{OA}=6\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\overrightarrow{OB}=6\underset{\sim}{b}$. The points $M$ and $N$ are the midpoints of $OA$ and $OB$, respectively. Find $\overrightarrow{MN}$ and use vectors to prove that $MN$ is parallel to $AB$. Assume $A$ and $B$ are distinct.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at (5,0); \coordinate (B) at (1,3); \coordinate (M) at (2.5,0); \coordinate (N) at (0.5,1.5);
\draw[black,thick,->] (O)--(A); \draw[black,thick,->] (O)--(B); \draw[black] (A)--(B); \draw[black,dashed] (M)--(N);
\fill[black] (M) circle (1.5pt); \fill[black] (N) circle (1.5pt);
\path (2.5,-0.65) node {$6\underset{\sim}{a}$} (-0.1,2.2) node[left] {$6\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\path (O) node[below left] {$O$} (A) node[below right] {$A$} (B) node[above] {$B$} (M) node[below] {$M$} (N) node[left] {$N$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$ABCD$ is a quadrilateral with $\overrightarrow{BA}=2\underset{\sim}{v}$, $\overrightarrow{AD}=3\underset{\sim}{w}$ and $\overrightarrow{CD}=\underset{\sim}{u}$. The point $M$ is the midpoint of $BC$. Find $\overrightarrow{MA}$ in terms of the given vectors.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0.5); \coordinate (B) at (4,0); \coordinate (C) at (4.8,2.6); \coordinate (D) at (1,3.2); \coordinate (M) at (4.4,1.3);
\draw[black,thick,->] (B)--(A) node[midway,below] {$2\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\draw[black,thick,->] (A)--(D) node[midway,left] {$3\underset{\sim}{w}$};
\draw[black,thick,->] (C)--(D) node[midway,above] {$\underset{\sim}{u}$};
\draw[black] (B)--(C); \fill[black] (M) circle (1.5pt);
\path (A) node[left] {$A$} (B) node[below right] {$B$} (C) node[above right] {$C$} (D) node[above left] {$D$} (M) node[right] {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
